riscv: boot the flash rescue root, not the microSD directly

Pairs with the Makefile change that makes the XIP image bootable (an /init and
six directories on an image that already carries busybox and its libraries).

The old line ended `root=/dev/mmcblk0 rootfstype=ext4 rw rootwait`, and
`rootwait` waits for ever. A card that is absent - or stuck busy after a warm
restart, see patches/0012 - left the board on "Waiting for root device
/dev/mmcblk0" with no console and no diagnosis.

Now the kernel mounts the flash cramfs, which is always there, and /init hands
over to the card when it appears (20 s limit) or drops to a shell and says why.
The card, when present, supersedes it completely: / is /dev/mmcblk0 ext4 rw and
every service starts exactly as before.

`ro` because cramfs is read-only anyway, and the card is mounted rw by /init.

--- a/arch/riscv/configs/esp32s31_defconfig
+++ b/arch/riscv/configs/esp32s31_defconfig
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@
 CONFIG_FPU=y
 
 # Kernel command line
-CONFIG_CMDLINE="dw_mmc.lost_irq_poll=0 dw_mmc.low_pwr=0 console=tty0 console=ttyS0,1000000n8 root=/dev/mmcblk0 rootfstype=ext4 rw rootwait init=/init profile=6"
+CONFIG_CMDLINE="dw_mmc.lost_irq_poll=0 dw_mmc.low_pwr=0 console=tty0 console=ttyS0,1000000n8 root=mtd:rootfs rootfstype=cramfs ro init=/init profile=6"
 CONFIG_CMDLINE_FORCE=y
 
 # Built-in DTB (no external loader needed)
